# HAZARD for anything that shells out to `git check-ignore`: a blank line here --
# and, on current git, a whitespace-only line or a lone CR left by CRLF -- is
# reported as a match for ANY path ending in "/". So a bare "docs/nowhere/" reads
# back "ignored" whether or not anything ignores it. A tool that treats
# "gitignored" as "not repository content, absence is fine" then waves through
# every broken directory reference. Do NOT delete the blank separators below to
# dodge this -- they are idiomatic. The fix is to never ask about a trailing-slash
# path: strip the slash and probe a non-"/" child instead. The one existing
# consumer, tools/instruction_refs/check_instruction_references.py:is_git_ignored,
# already does this; any new consumer must go through the same discipline. See
# tools/updater/README.md and issue #170.
node_modules/
*.log

# Python (tools/updater)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.venv-*/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Drydock
.drydock/tmp/

# Local tooling
.claude/settings.local.json
.docks/

# Data refresh run state (evidence bundles, gate output, PR/issue bodies)
.modeltree-refresh/
